  "question": {
    "text": "The centres of a set of circles, each of radius 3 , lie on the circle $x^2+y^2=25$. The locus of any point in the set is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QNT94",
      "text": "\n$4 \\leq x^2+y^2 \\leq 64$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "fIhl1",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2 \\leq 25$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YIKKY",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2 \\geq 25$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FzalW",
      "text": "\n$3 \\leq x^2+y^2 \\leq 9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $(h, k)$ be the centre of any such circle. Equation of such circle is $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=3^2$. Since $(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})$ lies on $\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2=25 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{h}^2+\\mathrm{k}^2=25$.\n$x^2+y^2-(2 x h+2 y k)+25=9$; Locus of $(h, k)$ is $x^2+y^2=16$, which clearly satisfies (a).",
    "image": null
  },
